Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||09-21-2000||09:14 AM||||As much fun as everyone here seems to make of imports, some of them can be pretty peppy right off the boat.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BellaFiero||09-21-2000||10:17 AM||||I think it's kind of tasteless to make fun of a car that you've never driven - that you've never owned. Just because it's made by a particular manufacturer doesn't really mean all that much to me. I judge the car's drivability. I don't care how fast it can go, or how many options are in it. I want a comfortable ride, with a sleek exterior. Honda Civics were never meant to go fast, huh? Yeah, well, doesn't that prove that some of the "Rice Boys" out there are doing some pretty amazing things with "slow" Civics? Have you seen the quarter mile times these guys are pulling? I'll be the first to admit that several Civics can ghost me off the line. Civics were never meant to go fast? Says who? Who said that? <P>...The same guy who said Fieros aren't sports cars. The same guy who points at a heavy-bass-hitting, lowered, tinting, neoned Civic and says 'that's a Rice Boy' ... um... last time I checked, there are more girls around here that do that sort of thing than guys with their Hondas. Besides, for all the bass and the neon and stickers, you don't know what's under that hood. Those bumble-exhausts may sound annoying, but they're better than those scraggly half inch diameter pipes that come factory. "Rice" can't be classified anymore - If I put a "Fiero" windshield banner on my car, that's cool. But if I put "Powered by Pontiac", the world calls it rice. We all need to stop judging others cars and concentrate on our own. I am sick and tired of people passing down judgement on so-called Rice Boys. How the hell do you know anything about that person? I happen to like the Rice-look and have incorporate it modestly into my own Fiero. Which, if anyone cares, will have it's pictures on-line tomorrow! <BR>Take it easy everyone.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||09-21-2000||10:26 AM||||the current Prelude's are actually very nice cars.  i tried to buy a used one, in '98, but  the dealer wouldnt give my much for my RX-7.  i really wanted that car... it was so fun to drive.<P>the eclipse AWD turbo's were very nice also.  the "cheap" ones are no where near the car.<P>when my current lease on my Jeep is up, i wouldnt be surprised to wind up in something like the new celica or prelude... if i buy a new car.<P>i am also considering the advantage of owning a '65 Ford T-bird convertible as a daily driver  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||09-21-2000||10:49 AM||||One of the reasons used for slamming rice boys is just down to earth patriotizm.  You know, "Buy American!"  Now a days that's tough when you read the fine print and it says,"Made in Japan by Mitsubishi".  Oh well just keep the coffee cans off the end of your exhaust. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
