Z||000009||2xsess||09-21-2000||01:10 PM||||I traded my 88GT T-top in on an 92 Prelude Si. I loved the Prelude, it was fast, and it handled like a dream. But I always missed my Fiero. I agree with a little bit of what everyone said. Bella was right on the money. Can't judge a car by reading a magazine, just think how many people wouldn't buy Fieros after reading the Automobile mag article. I also agree that the coffee can tail pipes are outrageous.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||09-21-2000||01:36 PM||||I figure unless you have a big block V8, anything over 3" for an exhaust is too big...<BR>personally I doubt I'd ever go over 2.5", which is only slightly larger than the stock Fiero tips.. right?<P>though, I do agree that a slightly larger tip looks better on imports than the drinking straws they come with.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> just not *too* big.. then it looks silly.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
