Z||000013||frontal lobe||09-21-2000||02:41 PM||||Honda makes excellent cars.  They may or may not be "your flavor", but they are excellent.  I personally can't warm up to the prelude styling, but if you do, then great.  A lot of fwd cars still handle well.  Have fun with it.  I'm sure you will get many trouble-free miles from it.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Black88GT||09-21-2000||10:40 PM||||I think everyone can agree that there is nothing wrong with stock Honda's, or even mildly modded ones.  But the people who spend thousands upon thousands in body kits, stickers, annoying exhausts and worthless "performance" mods are the ones we all love to hate.  Personally, I would have went with the Integra Type R before the Prelude SH.  But whatever floats your boat as they say.  Just for the sake of argument, I have an '88 Accord in my family and I have to say I am pretty impressed with the way it handles.  However it kinda sucks when I have to merge on the highway.  It makes a good daily driver though.    <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||7
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||09-23-2000||07:08 PM||||I was in a mall today with my sister, and I saw a 2001 Prelude..<P>my god it looked sweet!!! I had no idea Honda could make a car that looked that nice!! If I was ever going to buy a Japanese sports car, I'd get either a prelude.. an acura integra, a mazda mx-3 or a mitsubishi 3000GT..<P>anyway, my point is.. the new Preludes look NICE..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
